DESCRIPTION:All discussions must be submitted every Sunday at 6:00 p.m. (th
 is includes original postings and replies) for attendance purposes.\n\nT
 his discussion activity will include creating a new discussion board threa
 d.\n\nDiscuss "how public key cryptography works to protect the symmetric 
 keys that are used to protect data."\n\nRead chapter 11\, research\, think
  and learn more about public key cryptography.  This is a 3-part assignme
 nt (1 new thread and 2 replies)\, and all 3 parts will be considered for g
 rading.\n\nProofreading counts as part of the assignment grade\; points wi
 ll be deducted for spelling and grammar errors. Be specific -- details are
  important. Your entry should be substantive and meaningful. Include the f
 ull working URL of any online sources used.\n\nDiscussion Posting and Grad
 ing Criteria\n\nInitial discussion post (8 sentences)\n\n60% of overall cr
 edit\n\n2 replies to two other students (5 sentences each) 30% each\n\n30%
  of overall credit\n\nGrammar/spelling\n\n10% of overall credit\n\nTo subm
 it your responses to the questions\, follow the steps below:\n\n* Click Re
 ply at the bottom\, and post your responses to both questions in the same
  thread.  Be sure to click Post Reply at the bottom of the screen when y
 ou have completed your response.  If you click Save Draft\, your messag
 e cannot be viewed by the instructor or other students.\n\n* As other stud
 ents post their opinions\, read through the forum\, and respond to at leas
 t two other messages by clicking Reply to the student's post\, and Po
 st Reply.  The first couple of students who post messages may have to che
 ck back later to post their replies.
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY: Public key cryptography  [26/SP NET-313-OL01]
