DESCRIPTION:All discussions must be submitted every Sunday at 6:00 p.m. (th
 is includes original postings and replies) for attendance purposes.\n\nT
 his discussion activity will include creating a new discussion board threa
 d.\n\nDiscuss "Nano Server deployments. In what types of environments and 
 for what applications might Nano Server resolve currently existing problem
 s?\n\nRead the chapters\, research\, think and learn more about Nano Serve
 r.  This is a 3-part assignment (1 new thread and 2 replies)\, and all 3 
 parts will be considered for grading.\n\nProofreading counts as part of th
 e assignment grade\; points will be deducted for spelling and grammar erro
 rs. Be specific -- details are important. Your entry should be substantive
  and meaningful. Include the full working URL of any online sources used.\
 n\nDiscussion Posting and Grading Criteria\n\nInitial discussion post (8 s
 entences)\n\n60% of overall credit\n\n2 replies to two other students (5 s
 entences each) 30% each\n\n30% of overall credit\n\nGrammar/spelling\n\n10
 % of overall credit\n\nTo submit your responses to the questions\, follow 
 the steps below:\n\n* Click Reply at the bottom\, and post your responses
  to both questions in the same thread.  Be sure to click Post Reply at t
 he bottom of the screen when you have completed your response.  If you cl
 ick Save Draft\, your message cannot be viewed by the instructor or othe
 r students.\n\n* As other students post their opinions\, read through the 
 forum\, and respond to at least two other messages by clicking Reply to
  the student's post\, and Post Reply.  The first couple of students who
  post messages may have to check back later to post their replies.
